                Fact = "Big things in space are round because gravity pulls equally from every direction, squeezing them toward a ball shape. Small asteroids stay lumpy because their gravity is too weak to crush them round — you need to be about 600km wide before gravity wins." },
            new() { Topic = "What is a supernova",
