                Fact = "A supernova is a giant star's spectacular death: when it runs out of fuel, its core collapses and the star blows apart, briefly outshining an entire galaxy. The explosion scatters new elements into space — the calcium in your bones and iron in your blood were made in dying stars." },
            new() { Topic = "What is a neutron star",
