                Fact = "A neutron star is what's left after a supernova: the star's core crushed into a city-sized ball so dense that one teaspoon would weigh a billion tonnes. Some spin hundreds of times a second, sweeping beams of radio waves like a lighthouse — we call those pulsars." },
