                Fact = "A solar eclipse happens when the new moon passes exactly between Earth and the Sun and its shadow touches Earth. In the narrow path of a total eclipse, day turns to twilight for a few minutes. Never look at the Sun without proper eclipse glasses — even during most of an eclipse." },
            new() { Topic = "What a supermoon is",
