                Fact = "The moon's orbit isn't a perfect circle, so its distance changes through the month. A supermoon is a full moon that happens near its closest approach — it looks a little bigger and up to 30% brighter than the smallest full moons. The 'giant moon' you see near the horizon, though, is mostly a trick your brain plays." },
            new() { Topic = "What a blue moon is",
