                Fact = "A blue moon is the second full moon inside one calendar month. The moon's cycle takes about 29 and a half days, so most months fit only one full moon — a second one sneaks in roughly every two to three years. The moon doesn't actually turn blue; the name just means 'rare'." },
            new() { Topic = "The North Star",
                Keywords = new[] { "north star", "polaris", "find north", "star that never moves" },
