                Fact = "Venus is the hottest planet, around 465°C day and night — hot enough to melt lead. Mercury is closer to the Sun, but Venus's thick carbon-dioxide atmosphere traps heat like a runaway greenhouse, which is why it beats Mercury." },
            new() { Topic = "Coldest planet",
