                Fact = "Sunlight is a mix of every colour. Our air scatters blue light much more than red, bouncing blue all across the sky — so wherever you look up, blue is what reaches your eyes. At sunset the light crosses more air, the blue scatters away, and red and orange are left over." },
            new() { Topic = "What clouds are made of",
