                Fact = "On a truly dark night your eyes can pick out a few thousand stars. Our Milky Way galaxy holds over 100 billion, and the universe holds trillions of galaxies — more stars in total than grains of sand on all of Earth's beaches." },
            new() { Topic = "Sound in space",
