                Fact = "A telescope gathers far more light than your eye and magnifies whatever it points at. Even small backyard telescopes show Saturn's rings, Jupiter's moons and craters on our moon. The bigger the mirror or lens, the fainter and farther the things it reveals." },

            // ---------------- more dinosaur & prehistory science ----------------
            new() { Topic = "The word dinosaur",
