                Fact = "Most dinosaurs could probably paddle if they had to — fossil claw scrapes on ancient lake beds prove some did. Spinosaurus went much further: with its paddle tail and dense bones it hunted IN rivers — the closest thing to a truly swimming dinosaur." },
            new() { Topic = "Dinosaurs at the poles",
