                Fact = "Dinosaur fossils have been found on every continent — even Antarctica. Back then the poles were warmer and forested, but polar dinosaurs still faced months of winter darkness. Some may have grown fluffier feathers to keep warm." },
            new() { Topic = "Before the dinosaurs",
                Keywords = new[] { "before the dinosaurs", "what came before", "permian", "dimetrodon", "first animals on land" },
                Fact = "Before dinosaurs, Earth belonged to stranger creatures — giant dragonflies, metre-long millipedes, and sail-backed Dimetrodon, which was actually more closely related to YOU than to any dinosaur. A huge extinction 252 million years ago cleared the stage, and dinosaurs took over." },
            new() { Topic = "First life on Earth",
